<x-public-layout title="Refund Policy">
<article class="reference-container ats-guide policy-document">
<header class="ats-guide-intro"><span class="reference-eyebrow">CLEAR RULES FOR PURCHASES AND REFUNDS</span><h1>Refund Policy</h1><p class="policy-status">Effective date: 22 October 2026</p><p>This policy applies to verified purchases of atscvdetector digital plans and services. It balances fair remedies for customers with the cost of providing paid access and AI processing. For cancellations, payment problems and refund requests, email <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a>.</p></header>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>1. The main principles</h2><p>You pay for the advertised digital features, access and credit allowance, not a job offer, interview, employer response or guaranteed ATS score. We assess requests against the purchase description, verified payment, access provided, usage records and the reported issue.</p><p>Completed services and properly delivered paid access are generally not refundable simply because you change your mind. Voluntary purchase refunds are available only for eligible Annual plans under section 2. Billing mistakes, undelivered services and material defects are reviewed for correction and any remedy required by applicable law. Mandatory cancellation, cooling-off, refund and consumer rights take priority over every exclusion or time limit below. This is not a blanket "all sales final" policy.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>2. Annual plans only: seven-day unused-purchase refund</h2><p><strong>Monthly and Pro monthly plans are non-refundable, including unused purchases and renewals, except for billing corrections or refunds required by applicable law.</strong> Cancelling a monthly plan stops future renewal; it does not refund the current paid period.</p><p>For your first Annual plan purchase, you may request a full change-of-mind refund within <strong>seven calendar days of verified payment</strong> if none of that purchase's credits has been consumed and you have not used paid-only template access to save or download a CV. Viewing your plan, or payment verification alone, does not count as using a paid benefit.</p><p>This voluntary goodwill window applies only to the first Annual plan purchase, once per customer. It does not apply to Monthly or Pro monthly plans, new accounts created to repeat a claim, renewals or later Annual purchases. Deleting results after using paid benefits does not make the purchase unused. Separately purchased top-ups, where offered, do not receive this goodwill window unless expressly stated at checkout. These conditions do not restrict stronger statutory rights or remedies for defective services.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>3. Duplicate, incorrect or unauthorised charges</h2><p>If the same order is charged twice in error, we will refund the confirmed duplicate in full. If we charged more than the amount you authorised, we will correct the difference. Separate authorised orders are not automatically duplicate charges; contact support promptly if you accidentally placed the same order twice.</p><p>Report suspected unauthorised payments immediately to support and your payment provider or bank. We will investigate transaction and account records and cooperate with the relevant dispute process. Never disclose banking passwords, PINs or full card details. An amount already reversed or recovered will not be refunded a second time.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>4. Payment received but plan or credits missing</h2><p>If the provider confirms a successful payment but the app still shows Free or the wrong credit balance, email your transaction reference and account email. Please do not pay again merely to activate the same purchase. A pending payment or bank authorisation may require provider confirmation before allocation.</p><p>For a verified purchase, we will investigate and correct missing access or credits. If we cannot supply what you purchased within a reasonable time, we will provide any refund or other remedy required by applicable law. An immediate statutory remedy does not require you to wait for repeated correction attempts. A failed or unverified transaction cannot be treated as a completed payment without confirmation, but we can help investigate its status.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>5. Failed AI requests and technical defects</h2><p>An AI request that fails without delivering its result should not permanently consume its reserved credits. The app records reservations and failures; contact support if a reversal or displayed balance appears incorrect. Credit restoration corrects a failed operation and is different from refunding the subscription payment.</p><p>For an isolated recoverable issue, we may offer corrected output, a repeat operation, restored credits or restored access where appropriate and legally permitted. We will not require endless retries. For a material fault that cannot be remedied within a reasonable time or substantially prevents use of the purchased service, we will provide the monetary remedy required by applicable law. Restored credits do not replace a cash refund when one is legally required.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>6. Completed work and situations normally excluded</h2><ul class="ats-guide-checklist"><li><strong>Used credits:</strong> correctly completed analysis or rewriting is normally non-refundable because processing has already been supplied.</li><li><strong>Paid benefits used:</strong> changing your mind after saving or downloading with a paid-only template does not normally qualify for the Annual unused-purchase refund.</li><li><strong>Employment outcomes:</strong> a low score, no interview, employer rejection or lack of a job offer alone is not grounds for a refund.</li><li><strong>Personal preferences:</strong> disliking otherwise correctly described wording or a template after use does not by itself establish a defect.</li><li><strong>Unused allowance:</strong> choosing not to use a plan, forgetting to cancel, allowing credits to expire or buying more than needed does not automatically create a refund right.</li><li><strong>Input and device issues:</strong> an unrelated job description, inaccurate information you supplied or unsupported files do not by themselves establish a service fault. Misleading compatibility information or genuine import defects will still be reviewed.</li><li><strong>Free benefits:</strong> welcome credits, complimentary credits and free tools have no cash purchase price to refund.</li></ul><p>These exclusions do not excuse incorrect billing, misleading descriptions or material failure to provide the purchased service. Using AI or downloading output does not automatically waive statutory rights. Any legally required consent for immediate supply must be obtained separately; this policy alone is not that consent.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>7. Monthly plans, annual plans and renewals</h2><p>Cancelling automatic renewal stops future scheduled charges once cancellation is confirmed; it does not automatically refund the current term. Unless a refund or reversal changes your entitlement, access normally continues until that paid term ends. Email support if a cancellation control is unavailable.</p><p>Annual purchases cover a yearly term, with 2,400 credits added after verified payment and available until the paid term ends. The annual discount does not create a promise of monthly cash withdrawals or refunds for every unused month. Only an eligible first Annual purchase receives the seven-day unused-purchase refund window. Monthly and Pro monthly plans have no voluntary refund window. After the Annual window, we do not offer routine prorated change-of-mind refunds, except where applicable law or purchase terms require them.</p><p>Renewals do not receive a fresh first-purchase goodwill window. Report an incorrect renewal, a charge after a timely confirmed cancellation or an ongoing service failure promptly. We will investigate and refund amounts incorrectly charged or otherwise refundable by law. A one-time payment method does not create automatic renewal merely because a plan has a monthly or annual term.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>8. Partial delivery and service closure</h2><p>If only part of a paid service was properly supplied and a refund is due, we will explain how the refund reflects the affected or undelivered portion. Relevant factors may include the actual price paid, period of usable access, services delivered and the scope and duration of a verified fault. An unused credit balance alone is not a complete valuation of a subscription that also provides template access.</p><p>For example, if we permanently discontinue an annual service after six of twelve equal months were supplied and cannot offer an agreed suitable alternative, a time-based calculation would ordinarily refund six twelfths of the annual amount paid. A different legally required remedy takes priority. We will not retrospectively reprice used months at a higher monthly rate merely to eliminate a refund.</p><p>We do not deduct undisclosed administration penalties or automatically pass on our AI or payment-provider costs when a customer is entitled to a refund.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>9. When and how to request a review</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a> with "Refund request" as the subject. Include your account email, plan, payment date, amount and currency, provider transaction reference, what went wrong and your requested outcome. Relevant screenshots or error messages can help; redact unrelated information. Never send your password, PIN, full card number or security code.</p><p>Request an eligible Annual unused-purchase refund within its seven-day window. Monthly and Pro monthly purchases do not qualify for this voluntary refund. For our voluntary review of service problems, contact us within <strong>14 calendar days of payment or discovering the problem, whichever is later</strong>. This assists investigation and does not shorten statutory claim periods, cooling-off rights or payment-provider dispute deadlines.</p><p>We aim to acknowledge requests within five business days and provide a decision or progress update within fourteen business days. If we need further information or investigation time, we will explain. Shorter deadlines required by law take priority.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>10. How approved refunds are paid</h2><p>We normally refund to the original payment method in the original transaction currency. If that route is unavailable, we will agree a lawful secure alternative with the verified payer. We aim to initiate an approved refund within ten business days, or sooner where required by law. The payment provider and bank control any additional posting time.</p><p>We refund the approved amount of the original charge, not a guaranteed value in another currency. Exchange-rate changes or independent bank fees may affect what your bank displays. We do not deduct undisclosed refund fees. A payment already reversed by a provider will be reconciled rather than refunded twice.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>11. Credits, access and prevention of misuse</h2><p>A full plan refund normally removes the paid entitlement and credits supplied by that purchase. A partial refund may adjust only the relevant access or credits. Existing CV content is not automatically deleted as a penalty for requesting a refund, although future paid access depends on the remaining entitlement.</p><p>We may check payment and usage records to prevent double recovery, repeated goodwill claims through multiple accounts or reuse of refunded credits. We may decline a voluntary goodwill request supported by false information, subject to applicable rights. Legitimate complaints are assessed on their merits; a good-faith dispute is not proof of fraud.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>12. Review of decisions and legal rights</h2><p>If you disagree with a decision, reply to <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a> with "Refund review", the transaction reference and further evidence. We will explain our decision and reconsider relevant new information. Contacting us does not require you to give up a lawful bank dispute, court claim or complaint to a competent consumer authority.</p><p>Changes apply prospectively and do not retrospectively remove rights attached to earlier purchases. Read this alongside our <a href="{{ route('terms') }}">Terms and Conditions</a> and <a href="{{ route('privacy') }}">Privacy Policy</a>.</p></section>
</article>
